\par\par \b \uc2  Israel says no change is planned in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  regime. \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 4 (Reuter) - Finance Minister Dan Meridor and Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel said on Tuesday that they planned no changes in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system. \par \par \uc2  "There is no change in the exchange rate system," Meridor said after a meeting with Frenkel. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel vowed to continue to defend the exchange rate even though that has forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject more than an estimated $1 billion during January \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to defend the system," he said. "We have all the tools required to do this and we will continue to do so. Every dollar the Bank of Israel buys and the shekels we consequently sell we are absorbing immediately." \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded quietly on Tuesday and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Since mid-January, the shekel has been trading at the bottom end of its trading band against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which it is pegged. To prevent it from sliding under the band, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The financial daily Globes quoted senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials as saying they were considering various measures to alleviate pressure on the Bank of Israel to support the exchange rate and absorb the liquidity created by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Among them was a special tax on short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing; widening the trading band, which now allows the shekel to deviate up to seven percent above or below a sloping rate to as much as 12 percent; suspending further government borrowing overseas; and increasing the reserve requirement by five percentage points. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel expressed concern about the unexpectedly wide budget deficit in January, which reached 1.28 billion shekels. \par \par \uc2  "When in January the budget figures are so worrisome following so great an effort by the government (to approve the 1997 budget), it is very important that the budget cut which was decided upon is in fact implemented," Frenkel said. \par \par \uc2  "What happened in January is a result that troubles us very much," he said. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.32 shekels) \par \par \uc2  - Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2402ymq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
