\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel says no moves planned on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 4 (Reuter) - The Bank of Israel is not holding formal talks with the Treasury or working on a package of proposals to ease pressure on the shekel exchange rate, a spokesman for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "There are always discussions going on at the Bank of Israel, but there is no package of proposals being formulated," a spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  His remarks come before a scheduled meeting between Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel and Finance Minister Dan Meridor later today. Sources at the bank and Treasury said they doubted the meeting would produce any concrete proposals. \par \par \uc2  Since mid-January, the Israeli shekel has been trading at the bottom end of its trading band against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which it is pegged. To prevent it from sliding under the band, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent less than $100 million to support the basket rate. On Sunday a Treasury official said the bank had spent more than $1 billion during January \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The financial daily Globes quoted senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials as saying they were considering various measures to alleviate pressure on the Bank of Israel to support the exchange rate. Among them was a special tax on short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing. \par \par \uc2  The others include widening the trading band, which now allows the shekel to deviate up to seven percent above or below a sloping rate, to as much as 12 percent; suspending further government borrowing overseas and increasing the reserve requirement by five percentage points. \par \par \uc2  Bank officials said they are also seeking a further 1.3 billion shekel cut in the government's budget for 1997 after Treasury officials on Monday said tax revenues for January were behind projections. \par \par \uc2  They said tax and other revenues were only 8.6 billion shekels for the month, about 500 million shekels below the amount forecasted. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 3.32 shekels) \par \par \uc2  - Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2402yks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
