\par\par \b \uc2  Israel: Shekel Trading Band System Under Fire \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1997\par 19:19\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)-- Israeli economists are engaged in a intense debate about the future of the country's rate of exchange regime, as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily to prevent a strong appreciation of the shekel. \par \par \uc2  According to unofficial calculations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced during the past four weeks to purchase about $1.3 bn in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. To prevent a major increase in money supply, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to increase deposits of commercial banks. The Bank of Israel has also asked the Finance Ministry to allow it to sell a larger amounts of Treasury Bills, but the ministry has refused to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of this matter, according to government official talking on the basis of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  ``The Bank should not do away with the trading band system. Instead it should devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  administratively and announce that it will do the same in the future. That would introduce risk into the markets and prevent selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 '', said Ptahia Bar Shavit, chief economist at Bank Hapoalim. He added that the system of a trading band had served the economy very well and should be kept. \par \par \uc2  Other economists were critical of the trading band system. According to Sauli Katznelson, chief economist at Israel Discount Bank the solution the the problem would be to do away with the trading band. Officialy there would be a free floating shekel, but in practice there would be incrased risk, and much smaller speculative import of short term capital, he said. \par \par \uc2  -Avi Temkin \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 03-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1819GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt23000wu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
