\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Reach Record $12.8 Bln \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1997\par 14:47\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)-- The Bank of Israel, which bought more than $1 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to weaken the shekel, posted record foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $12.8 billion at the end of January. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased by $1.372 billion in January from $11.46 billion at the end of December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel attributed most of the rise to its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases and the government's capital sourcing abroad. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, Finance Ministry Director General David Brodet said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than $1 billion in January to weaken the shekel and keep it from strengthening to a point outside its trading band. \par \par \uc2  In January, the dollar was valued at anywhere from 3.2407 shekels to 3.3190 shekels, the Bank of Israel reported. On Jan. 31, the dollar traded at 3.3140 shekels. \par \par \uc2  By the end of January, the dollar had risen 25.36% against the shekel in nominal, annualized terms. In January, the dollar strengthened 1.94% in nominal terms, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is adjusted against a basket of five major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and in January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was valued between 3.6119 and 3.6411 shekels, the Bank of Israel reported. By the end of the month, the shekel had strengthened 2.62% against the basket in nominal, annualized terms; by the end of the month it had strengthened 0.23% against the basket in nominal terms. \par \par \uc2  Because the shekel has strengthened so much against this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 02-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1347GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt22000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
