\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Discount Rate -4: Critics Demand Deeper Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1997\par 16:11\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The president of the Manufacturers Association of Israel, Dan Propper, urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abandon its "wrong-headed monetary policy" and to lower the key interest by about two percentage points. \par \par \uc2  Bank Governor Jacob Frenkel is pursuing a tight monetary policy for fear that significantly lower interest rates would depreciate the strong shekel and fuel inflation. \par \par \uc2  As far as inflation goes, Frenkel's strategy has been successful: Inflation was tamped down from about 16% in annualized terms in the first six months of 1996 to about 6% in annualized terms in the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  But the cost to the economy has been high. Business profits and exports have suffered because of the strong shekel. And the capital market has been hurt because many investors have preferred to put their money in savings accounts that bear high interest rather than risk investing it on the stock exchange. \par \par \uc2  The government has projected that gross domestic product grew 4.4% in 1996, a sharp drop from 7.1% in 1995 and an average of 6% annually from 1990 to 1995. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry economists have fovecast a 4% GDP growth in 1997, but other economists have projected that the economy will grow around 3%. \par \par \uc2  This month the governor has been under even greater pressure to lower the discount rate because the high rate has strengthened the shekel beyond its strongest point in the trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set. \par \par \uc2  This has forced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading this month to weaken the shekel. By several estimates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought some $800 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 27-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1511GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt1r0046b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
