\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel lowers interest rates 0.5 point. \b0\par\par\uc2  By David Rosenberg \par \uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 1997\par 18:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 27 (Reuter) - The Bank of Israel said on Monday it would lower its key lending rate for February, but analysts and traders said the 0.5 percentage point cut was cautious and would do little to ease pressure on the shekel exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The cut, which takes effect on Thursday, brings the base lending rate to 14.2 percent. The rate is the one charged commercial banks at daily and weekly monetary tenders. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had cut rates 2.8 percentage points since August from a peak of 17 percent. But inflation has fallen from a 14.6 percent annualised rate in the first-half of 1996 to less than half that in the second, according to Bank Hapoalim estimates. \par \par \uc2  "It was (the reduction) expected, no surprises. They put a lot of pressure on (Bank of Israel Governor Jacob) Frenkel to lower more but he was very cautious. It won't influence shares or the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Tzvi Hoffman of Meitav Securities and Investments. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank faces pressure to keep lowering rates to prevent the shekel from strengthening too much against the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which it is officially linked. The bank sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band as a key facet in achieving monetary stability. \par \par \uc2  The shekel on Monday fell to an all-time low against the dollar. However, the weakness of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket has caused the basket rate to fall over the last two weeks to the bottom end of its official trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, injecting what \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimated was about $500 million into the economy. \par \par \uc2  Jonathan Katz, chief economist at Solid Financial Markets, said the lower inflationary trend and a slowing economy were also encouraging the bank to ease rates. \par \par \uc2  The slowing trend has recently grown worse, with the Bank of Israel's "S" index of economic performance falling one percent over November and December. \par \par \uc2  Katz is now forecasting that the economy will grow three percent this year, down from the 3.7 percent he had earlier forecast. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must also contend with the budget deficit, which analysts said was making it cautious. Although the official budget aims to keep the deficit to 2.8 percent of gross domestic product, analysts said January spending was probably running ahead of projections. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1r0109l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
