\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Israel/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Wider Band Mooted Informally \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1997\par 17:07\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket traded at 3.6206 shekels Monday, down from 3.6354 shekels at the end of December, after the Bank of Israel bought an estimated $100 million to $150 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has soaked up the liquidity generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing Treasury bills and using other monetary tools, so the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not contributing to inflation, local banking sources said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , other than to say that it is committed to protecting its exchange-rate band. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Israel officials have informally raised the possibility of widening the trading band, one source in the local banking community said. But that decision would have to be taken in conjunction with the Finance Ministry, which opposes a wider band. \par \par \uc2  In any case, widening the band only slightly would merely delay \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a few days, the manager of one local bank's trading room said. If the band were widened significantly, imports would become more expensive, fueling inflation, and exports would become far less competitive, he added. \par \par \uc2  But while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  costs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  money, it can keep up the activity for some time, onlookers say. \par \par \uc2  "They will protect (the shekel's trading band) as much as necessary," Bank Hapoalim's Viskin said. "They won't have any problem protecting it. They have the money." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel counted foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $11.46 billion at Dec. 31, up from $8.16 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 21-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1607GMT \par \par \uc2  1142 1802 1805 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt1l002y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
