\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Israel Buying Brings Shekel Back In Trading Band \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1997\par 18:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)-- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Tuesday, but didn't have to buy much foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel enough to bring it within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed down 0.011% against the basket of major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which it is adjusted. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket traded at 3.6210 shekels at the fixing, compared to 3.6206 shekels on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is dominated by the dollar, and the Bank of Israel fixes rates for both the dollar and the basket each session. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the shekel closed up 0.091% against the dollar, however, trading at 3.2840 to the dollar, compared to 3.2870 to the dollar at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded within a very narrow range of 3.2840-3.2880 shekels, said Ron Bedny, manager of the dollar-shekel desk at Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  'It was a quiet day,' said Norbert Brinker, president of Gift Ltd., a portfolio management company. 'The dollar calmed down across the world, looking for a base from which to rise.' \par \par \uc2  Because trading volume was so small, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to weaken the shekel and bring it back within the trading band, Bedny said. \par \par \uc2  Bedny estimated that the Bank of Israel bought $40 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Monday, dealers estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $100 million to $150 million to bring the shekel back into the trading band. \par \par \uc2  To moderate cycles of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation that were fueled by expectations of devaluation, Israel linked the shekel to a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1986. The dollar is weighted heaviest, accounting for about 60% of the basket. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket exchange rate is allowed to fluctuate 7% in each direction from a midpoint. The shekel has been pushing the strongest point of its trading band for several weeks becasue of a 14.7% discount rate that has attracted investors to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1719GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1l00fcy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
