\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel little changed against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 21 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed almost unchanged against the dollar and the basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was traded slightly lower abroad and this led to a mild rise of the shekel against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The basket was almost unchanged after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading to raise the basket to seven percent below the diagonal rate," said a dealer at Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a trading band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Companies are using the opportunity of the strong dollar to sell them knowing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to buy dollars to support the basket," the dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 320 million shekels in dollars on Monday to support the basket, as the dollar rose to 3.2870 shekels from 3.2700 on Friday. Traders said the extent of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today was considerably lower. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.2840 shekels against 3.2870 shekels on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6210 shekels against 3.6206 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7871 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7876 on Monday and against the mark at 2.0255 shekels against 2.0206 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.2830 shekels. \par \par \uc2  Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1l03p2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
