\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel fixed slightly higher against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 16 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was fixed slightly higher against the dollar on Thursday following the weakening of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel was steady, trading in a narrow range during most of the day and rising slightly after the dollar weakened mildly against the mark and yen," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The weakening of the dollar prevented the basket from falling further. The basket was stuck at around 6.92 percent below the diagonal rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a trading band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the basket rate was touching bottom, dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market today. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market in three of the last six trading sessions in a bid to keep the basket rate within the band, buying what dealers estimated was about 500 million shekels in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.2630 shekels against 3.2680 shekels on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6186 shekels against 3.6185 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7865 shekels per 100 yen against 2.7835 on Wednesday and against the mark at 2.0510 shekels against 2.0451 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.2640 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1g04zg5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
