\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Shekel \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1997\par 18:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading again on Tuesday to weaken the shekel and keep it within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened slightly against major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at 3.2590 shekels to the dollar, an appreciation of 0.092% compared with Monday's close of 3.2620 shekels. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dominates the basket of five major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against which the shekel is adjusted. On Tuesday, the shekel strengthened 0.055% against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, which traded at 3.6172 shekels at the fixing, compared with 3.6192 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  For weeks, the shekel has been hovering around the strongest point in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. Last week, the shekel strengthened to a point outside the band, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading for the first time in about four months to weaken the shekel and bring it back within the band. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened beyond the band again on Tuesday, and about half an hour before the fixing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the shekel within the band, said Ilan Engel of Koor Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought just enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the shekel within the band, and didn't weaken it much, said Sandrine Finkelstein of United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  Large companies have to pay value-added tax in the middle of the month so they convert dollars to shekels, strengthening the shekel, Finkelstein said. \par \par \uc2  Engel said the dollar went down after weakening against major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was very slow, and the dollar traded within a narrow range,\par both traders said.\par    -Amy Teibel\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-01-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1735GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1e00b90\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
