\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel stable as Bank of Israel buys dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 9 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel representative rate was almost unchanged against the dollar and the basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was very quiet today. The only active player in the market was the Bank of Israel," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading (buying dollars) after the basket fell by seven percent below the diagonal rate." \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate in a trading band of seven percent above or below a sloping mid-point designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a rate of six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought only about $17 million of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its first market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in five months. \par \par \uc2  "For the near term the basket will remain at the current level and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," the Hapoalim dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was fixed at 3.2480 shekels against 3.2470 shekels on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, was fixed at 3.6139 shekels against 3.6145 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.7949 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8040 on Wednesday and against the mark at 2.0598 shekels against 2.0636 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.2480 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1907vl8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
