\par\par \b \uc2  Israel's Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Up to $10.26 Bln \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1996\par 15:16\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--Israel's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $740 million to $10.262 billion at the end of September, in part because of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases the Bank of Israel made to protect its exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  The other factor contributing to the rise from $9.523 billion at the end of August were transfers of government money from overseas, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a release. \par \par \uc2  The bank gave no breakdown of its purchases versus transfers of money from overseas accounts, and a spokesman was not immediately available. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market did not add liquidity to the market "because every influence that contributes to the undesirable increase in the amount of money is completely offset by the variety of monetary tools the bank has at its disposal." \par \par \uc2  The statement did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  In late August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading for the first time since February, after its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket exchange rate dipped below the lowest point that the Bank of Israel has said it will permit. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout September to prop up the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  To moderate cycles of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation that were fueled by expectations of devaluation, Israel linked the shekel to a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1986. The dollar is weighted heaviest, accouting for about 60% of the basket. \par \par \uc2  -Amy Teibel \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 01-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1316GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 1901 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsa100fjd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
