\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Weakens Against Israeli Shekel After Two-Day Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1996\par 14:38\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The dollar lost steam against the shekel on Tuesday, after rising 1.5% in the previous two days. Analysts said the drop was a correction of an extraordinary rise on Monday that appeared to have been a combined reaction to deadly Palestinian-Israeli clashes and the strengthening of the dollar around the world late last week. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the dollar opened with a decline of 0.67%, which drove down the dollar exchange rate to 3.19832 shekels, from 3.22 shekels on Monday. \par \par \uc2  About half an hour later it was down 0.9% to 3.1916, and at the end of a trading day shortened because of the Sukkot holiday, the Bank of Israel fixed the exchange rate at 3.1920, a drop of 0.87%. \par \par \uc2  Trading was much quieter than on Monday, when large morning purchases by banks and the commercial sector set off panicked buying that temporarily drove up the exchange rate to 3.24 shekels to the dollar, said Aviad Bar-Sella, a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  Monday's volatile trading was a delayed reaction to the violence that engulfed the West Bank and Gaza Strip last week, and Tuesday's drop in the dollar exchange rate was a return to business as usual, Bar-Sella said. \par \par \uc2  "There was profit-taking, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so rates went down," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket exchange rate from dipping below the lowest point the Bank of Israel has set. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 01-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1238GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsa100fio\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
