\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel weakens, unaffected by violence. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1996\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 26 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel on Thursday weakened against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the dollar's rise abroad and trade was not affected by the political unrest, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market did not react to the political events and the shekel weakened after the dollar rose abroad," said Ilan Raviv at Israel Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  In two days of bloody clashes between Israeli troops and Palestinians 33 Palestinians and five Israelis were killed. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a relatively high scale in the market, buying more than $50 million to support the basket. The market will be influenced by the political unrest between Israel and the Palestinians only if foreign investors decide to leave Israel," Raviv said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can trade in a band of seven percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1800 against 3.1710 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5567 shekels against 3.5541 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8795 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8774 on Wednesday and against the mark at 2.0920 shekels per mark against 2.1019 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1800 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9q02j4u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
