\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel up on dollar, weaker vs basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 25 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel rose mildly against the dollar but weakened slightly against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid conversions of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for end-of-the-month payments, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quiet today. The business sector was converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels for end-of-the-month payments. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to support the basket," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  "The representative rate for the basket was set at 6.97 percent below the slope. But after the setting of the representative rate the dollar and basket traded at a lower level," he said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can trade in a band of seven percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1710 against 3.1730 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5541 shekels against 3.5532 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8774 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8911 on Tuesday and against the mark at 2.1019 shekels per mark against 2.0967 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1695 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9p02lmz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
