\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel up against dlr, weaker vs basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 24 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel rose mildly against the dollar but weakened slightly against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday there was no foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in Israel because of the Jewish holiday of Yom Kippur. \par \par \uc2  "The market was very quiet with slightly more conversions of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a relatively high scale to support the basket," said Guy Levi at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  "Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the basket traded at the end of the day at 6.99 percent below the slope. The rate cut had no real impact on trading today," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel lowered its key lending rate for October by 0.3 percentage point to an annualised nominal rate of 15.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can trade in a band of seven percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1730 against 3.1740 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5532 shekels against 3.5516 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8911 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8887 on Friday and against the mark at 2.0967 shekels per mark against 2.0943 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1730 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9o02jsf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
