\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel weakens against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 10 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened against the dollar and the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the rise of the dollar abroad, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was quiet today. In early session the shekel declined against the dollar following the dollar's rise in Europe," said a dealer at Bank Discount. \par \par \uc2  "The basket fell lower than 7.0 percent below the slope and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, buying dollars to support the basket," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel declined today following the rise of the dollar against the mark. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a relatively high scale," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a trading band of 7.0 percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1610 against 3.1530 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5451 shekels against 3.5442 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8901 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8933 on Monday and against the mark at 2.1036 shekels per mark against 2.1135 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1605 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9a03cqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
