\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel little changed in quiet trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 5 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel closed almost unchanged against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but rose slightly against the dollar in quiet trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was extremely quiet today and nothing happened. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market until the setting of the representative rate," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  "Right after the setting of the representative rate the basket fell lower than 7.0 percent below the slope," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a very low scale just after the setting of the rate," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a trading band of 7.0 percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1440 against 3.1470 on Wednesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5422 shekels against 3.5423 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8831 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8886 on Wednesday and against the mark at 2.1235 shekels per mark against 2.1190 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1440 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9503fvc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
