\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel declines against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 3 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened mildly against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the basket, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quiet today. Once again the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when the basket fell below the lower range of the trading band," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "In late morning the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a low scale, but just before the setting of the representative rate it started buying on a larger scale," he added. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel declined against the dollar as the dollar rose abroad following the U.S. air strike in Iraq. When the dollar slipped from earlier highs the shekel rose mildly," a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a trading band of 7.0 percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against the basket, representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1480 against 3.1440 on Monday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5416 shekels against 3.5402 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8834 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8823 on Monday and against the mark at 2.1175 shekels per mark against 2.1210 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1480 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9303lki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
