\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel declines against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Sept 2 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened mildly against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following several \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "When the session opened the basket was trading at 7.08 percent below the slope. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market several times, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Gideon Sadeh at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a trading band of 7.0 percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  representing Israel's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  many times and on a higher scale than in the last few days. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the main player today," Sadeh said. \par \par \uc2  Figures published by the Bank of Israel show that since the beginning of 1996 the basket has lost 1.61 percent in annual terms. In August alone the basket lost 0.67 percent. The dollar has gained 0.33 percent in annual terms since the beginning of the year but fell 0.35 percent last month. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1440 against 3.1420 on Friday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5402 shekels against 3.5394 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8823 shekels per 100 yen against 2.8979 on Friday and against the mark at 2.1210 shekels per mark against 2.1230 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1460 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9203k2r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
