\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel weakens against dollar, basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 28 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened slightly against the dollar and basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the Bank bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  just before the close of the trading day and after the representative rate was published. It was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six months. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel was stable during the whole day and activity was relatively low. When the session opened, the basket was traded at 7.03 percent below the slope but then the shekel started falling following the rise of the dollar abroad," said a dealer at Discount Bank. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a band of 7.0 percent above or below a so-called slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket rate reaches the lower trading band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on a very low scale but it was enough and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again today," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1410 versus 3.1370 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, pound sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5392 shekels versus 3.5385 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.8989 shekels per 100 yen versus 2.9104 on Tuesday and against the mark at 2.1243 shekels per mark versus 2.1266 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1395 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8s03mul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
