\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervenes \highlight\uc2  in shekel trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 27 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the trading of the shekel on Tuesday by buying dollars, preventing the shekel from trading beyond the band within which it is allowed to fluctuate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "At the end of the trading day, after the representative rates were published, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought a few million dollars bringing the shekel rate against the basket (of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to 7.0 percent below the slope," said Israel Sapir, chief dealer at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The shekel can fluctuate in a trading band of 7.0 percent above or below a slope designed to devalue the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six percent a year against the basket of key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  If the shekel-basket exchange rate reaches the lower trading band the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sapir said that the shekel had been trading at 6.96 percent below the slope at the end of the day and after the representative rates were published, in trading between the banks the rate fell below 7.0 percent. Just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed its trading day it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and bought a small amount of dollars, Sapir said. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel brought the rate to 7.0 percent below the slope and this means it will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again tomorrow," said Sapir. "All in all this is not a change in the trend, but an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had to happen." \par \par \uc2  He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for six months. "I don't think rates will shoot up tomorrow, maybe go up slightly more because the public may think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to weaken the shekel. But this is certainly not a change in direction." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not confirm \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of this sort. \par \par \uc2  -Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8r03uk9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
