\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel buys dollars, shekel softens. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 21 (Reuter) - The shekel weakened against the dollar and the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in active inter-bank trading after the first Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two weeks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading opened with another slide of the dollar. Just before the end of the trading day the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying dollars, the first time in two weeks," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the fact the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on a very small scale, the major banks reacted immediately and the dollar rose in very active trading," he said. \par \par \uc2  "By mid-trading the dollar had fallen to 3.0820 shekels and then one of the big banks started buying on a big scale, a move followed by all the other banks," said a dealer at the First International Bank of Israel. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.0970 shekels against 3.0830 on Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5119 against 3.4987 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9375 shekels per 100 yen against 2.9195 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 2.1317 shekels per mark from 2.1267 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.0880 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2l016uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
