\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel stable vs dollar, gains on basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 31 (Reuter) - The shekel closed unchanged against the dollar but gained on the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel's rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quite volatile today. The business sector sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for end-of-the-month payments and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few times in the market, buying dollars, to keep the shekel stable and prevent it from rising," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.1400 shekels unchanged from Tuesday. The basket, composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.5245 against 3.5276 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9323 shekels per 100 yen against 2.9318 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 2.1063 shekels per mark from 2.1131 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1400 shekels. \par \par \uc2  (See page ILS= for latest commercial bank shekel/dollar rates, ILS1= for a list of commercial bank shekel/dollar rates, ILS2 for a list of commercial bank shekel/basket rates. Bank of Israel announcements appear on BOIJ). \par \par \uc2  - Dan Gerstenfeld, Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds1v01er4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
