\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel eases, budget cut, devaluation talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Nov 20 (Reuter) - Israelis rushed to buy dollars on Monday amid reports that a new Israeli government will cut the budget and devalue the shekel. \par \par \uc2  In the late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.1000 as against 3.0530 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Israeli newspapers speculated last week that Acting Prime Minister Shimon Peres will cut the budget by two billion shekels in exchange for an agreement by the Bank of Israel to lower its main lending rate to banks and devaluae the shekel. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied the reports, saying that despite its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Thursday and Friday the bank has not changed its policy in regard to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  "Activity was very strong. Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen in the market today the dollar rose sharply against the shekel following expectations for a new economic plan," said a dealer at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  "The shekel did weaken, but many big companies used the opportunity to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Maybe this time the dollar will remain stable at the 3.1000 level," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drbk01ofq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
