\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel buys dollars to contain shekel. \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Nov 16 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened against the dollar and the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading started with big conversions but then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few times on a very high scale. Following this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar rose by 0.7 percent and the basket by 0.6 percent," said a dealer at the First International Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market the big banks started also buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Maybe someone was trying to raise the representative rate because one of the major banks started selling dollars immediately after the representative rate was set," said a dealer at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.0300 against 3.0110 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9842 shekels per 100 yen as against 2.9805 on Wednesday and against the mark at 2.1561 from 2.1493 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drbg01wo3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
