\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Israel buys dollars, shekel weakens. \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Oct 25 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened for the third consecutive day against the dollar and a basket of key foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the Treasury criticised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for raising interest rates, which has led to the shekel's appreciation. Treasury Director General David Brodett said the shekel must depreciate by four to five percent. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel has said there will be no devaluation of the shekel but it is acting like there is one going on," a dealer at the First International Bank of Israel said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars led the market and in early trade the dollar's rate rose to above 3.0400 shekels. He noted that the dollar also recovered in Europe and Asia. \par \par \uc2  "During early trade a group of big banks acquired dollars and this was followed by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (buying dollars) and the dollar jumped. By mid-trade investors started selling dollars and the trend changed," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  The representative rate for the dollar was 3.0350 shekels against 3.0180 on Tuesday. The basket, which is composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.4941 shekels per basket unit against 3.4851 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded 3.0020 per 100 yen against 3.0172 on Tuesday and at 2.1720 shekels per mark from 2.1765 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.0350 shekels. \par \par \