\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel gains,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, March 21 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel strengthened against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket and major foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors continued to convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into shekels to take advantage of high domestic interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The business sector continued to convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which strengthened the shekel. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more heavily than yesterday and bought dollars," said Ilan Viskin of Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed the daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tender at 2.9530 shekels per dollar against 2.9860 on Monday. The basket, which is composed of the dollar, mark, sterling, French franc and yen, closed at 3.4259 shekels per basket unit against 3.4553 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 3.3219 shekels per 100 yen against 3.3283 on Monday and against the mark at 2.1138 shekels per mark from 2.1287 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 2.9560 shekels. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr3l09emc\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum